      "As digital technologies advance at an astonishing pace, more and more people are choosing to live in the virtual world rather than interact face to face. Where will this trend lead us? In my view, spending excessive time online is likely to reshape our lives in worrying ways.",
      "First, human relationships will probably grow more distant. Picture a family sitting in one room at dinner, yet each member is silently staring at a glowing screen, connected to strangers online but disconnected from those beside them. As such scenes multiply, our real social skills may gradually decay, since abilities like reading emotions and holding a warm conversation only sharpen through practice. What is more, constant immersion could damage both our mental and physical health, leaving many anxious, lonely and out of shape.",
      "This does not mean the virtual world is purely harmful; it can indeed link distant hearts and boost efficiency. Yet the key lies in balance. The more time we surrender to screens, the more deliberately we should return to reality. Only by keeping one foot firmly in the real world can we enjoy technology without being enslaved by it."
